1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,660
At the North Pole of Uranus,

2
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:04,059
the seventh planet in orbit around our Sun,

3
00:00:04,640 --> 00:00:05,480
what would you see

4
00:00:05,520 --> 00:00:07,780
when the Sun sinks below the horizon?

5
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,060
A single winter night

6
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:12,760
that lasts 21 Earth years.

7
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:14,960
While Earth spins

8
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:17,700
at a 23.44-degree tilt,

9
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:22,160
Uranus is tipped at 97.77 degrees,

10
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,800
more than four times Earth's tilt,

11
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:27,640
and nearly at a right angle to its orbit,

12
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:30,980
rolling around the Sun on its side like a ball.

13
00:00:31,340 --> 00:00:33,540
How did an entire giant planet

14
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,520
get knocked onto its side?
